<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLMs merging. </span> We present Llama 3 8B results in natural language inference in <a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.1 Results ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. In line with our complexity analysis, merging in Core Space is much more efficient than merging in Full or KnOTS space, bringing up to <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="600\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">600\times</annotation></semantics></math> merging speed-up. Moreover, merging in Core Space improves the performance of all tested merging methods. In particular, it elevates TSV to 94.16% average normalized accuracy, achieving state-of-the-art results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
