<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>No Information Loss in Core Space Representation</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Least Squares Solutions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the components of two low-rank matrices <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> represented in SVD form. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the shared <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">reference bases</span>, obtained by taking the left and the right singular vectors from the SVD of the horizontally and vertically stacked low-rank matrices <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively (see Eq. 4 in the main paper). We assume <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\leq m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tasks and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is LoRA rank, as both are typically small relative to the feature dimension. Then, the solutions to the least square problems:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}R_{B}^{(t)}=\argmin_{R\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}}\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2},\quad Q_{A}^{(t)}=\argmin_{Q\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}}\left\|{V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}Q-{V_{A}^{(t)}}\right\|_{F}^{2},\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msup><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}R_{B}^{(t)}=\argmin_{R\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}}\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2},\quad Q_{A}^{(t)}=\argmin_{Q\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}}\left\|{V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}Q-{V_{A}^{(t)}}\right\|_{F}^{2},\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">are given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)},\quad Q^{(t)}_{A}={V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)},\quad Q^{(t)}_{A}={V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> come from the SVDs of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, they are orthonormal:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V_{A}^{(t)}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}=I_{r}\qquad{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}=I_{r}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V_{A}^{(t)}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}=I_{r}\qquad{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}=I_{r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times r</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix. Similarly, the reference bases <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> also have orthonormal columns:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r},\qquad{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r},\qquad{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\times T\cdot r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\times T\cdot r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\times T\cdot r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\times T\cdot r</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the problems in <a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. Each objective is convex and admits a unique global minimizer, as <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> have full column rank due to their orthonormality. To solve the first problem, we compute the gradient of the objective function with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}}{\partial R}=2{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}}{\partial R}=2{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the gradient to zero and solving the resulting equation gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I_{T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for the second problem in <a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A}^{(t)}={V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A}^{(t)}={V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}V_{A}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Alignment Error Quantification</h3>

<div id="Thmlemmax3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmax3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmlemmax3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmax3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmax3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmax3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> be matrices with orthonormal columns where <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r=\mathrm{rank}([B^{(1)},\dots,B^{(T)}])\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r=\mathrm{rank}([B^{(1)},\dots,B^{(T)}])\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemmax3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B}^{(t)}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal solution minimizing the error of the least-square problem. Then, the optimal alignment error is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{U}=\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R_{B}^{(t)}-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}=r-\left\|{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\right\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{U}=\left\|U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}R_{B}^{(t)}-U_{B}^{(t)}\right\|_{F}^{2}=r-\left\|{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\right\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To derive the alignment error, we simplify the notation by temporarily omitting the dependency on the model index <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting the definition <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B}={U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A1.E15" title="In A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we can write:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{U}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=||U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}-U_{B}||_{F}^{2}=||(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}||_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}-U_{B}||_{F}^{2}=||(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}||_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\left[(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}\right]^{\top}\left[(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\left[(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}\right]^{\top}\left[(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})U_{B}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})^{2}U_{B}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-I_{m})^{2}U_{B}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-2U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}+I_{m})U_{B}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-2U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}+I_{m})U_{B}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-2U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}+I_{m})U_{B}\right)\quad\quad(\text{by using }\ {U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>by using </mtext><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}-2U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}+I_{m})U_{B}\right)\quad\quad(\text{by using }\ {U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}=I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(I_{m}-U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top})U_{B}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}(I_{m}-U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top})U_{B}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left({U_{B}}^{\top}U_{B}\right)-\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}\right)\quad\quad\quad\quad\ \text{(by linearity of trace)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext>(by linearity of trace)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left({U_{B}}^{\top}U_{B}\right)-\mathrm{tr}\left(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B}\right)\quad\quad\quad\quad\ \text{(by linearity of trace)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r-\left\|U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\right\|_{F}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r-\left\|U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\right\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B})=\|U_{B}\|_{F}^{2}=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B})=\|U_{B}\|_{F}^{2}=r</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> has orthonormal columns, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B})=\|U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}{U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}}^{\top}U_{B})=\|U_{B}^{\top}U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by the cyclic property of the trace and definition of the Frobenius norm.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Optimal Reference Bases</h3>

<div id="Thmlemmax4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemmax4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmlemmax4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemmax4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemmax4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmax4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A solution <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to the quadratic program:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{U\in\mathcal{S}}\left\|{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U\right\|_{F}^{2}=\max_{U\in\mathcal{S}}\mathrm{tr}\left(U^{\top}{U_{B}^{(t)}}{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U\right),\quad\mathcal{S}=\left\{U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}\;\middle|\;U^{\top}U=I_{T\cdot r}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>U</mi><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mi>tr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>U</mi><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{U\in\mathcal{S}}\left\|{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U\right\|_{F}^{2}=\max_{U\in\mathcal{S}}\mathrm{tr}\left(U^{\top}{U_{B}^{(t)}}{U_{B}^{(t)}}^{\top}U\right),\quad\mathcal{S}=\left\{U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}\;\middle|\;U^{\top}U=I_{T\cdot r}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemmax4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemmax4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is given by any orthonormal basis whose columns include the top <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvectors corresponding to nonzero eigenvalues of <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}{B^{(t)}}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>B</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}{B^{(t)}}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> or, equivalently, by the top <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> left singular vectors of <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. At the optimum, the objective achieves the maximum value of <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding zero alignment error
in <math id="Thmlemmax4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Lemma. ‣ A.2 Alignment Error Quantification ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in two steps. First, we show that any orthonormal basis <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> containing the top <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvectors of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> solves the optimization problem. Second, we establish that the eigenvectors of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> are the same as those of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Solving the constrained optimization. </span> By leveraging the method of Lagrange multipliers, we write the augmented objective function:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)=\mathrm{tr}(U^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U)-\mathrm{tr}\left(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)=\mathrm{tr}(U^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U)-\mathrm{tr}\left(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> is a matrix of Lagrange multipliers. Taking gradients with respect to <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{U}\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>U</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{U}\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial U}\mathrm{tr}(U^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U)-\frac{\partial}{\partial U}\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial U}\mathrm{tr}(U^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U)-\frac{\partial}{\partial U}\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U-2U\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U-2U\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\Lambda}\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\Lambda}\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}))=U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\Lambda}\mathcal{L}(U,\Lambda)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\Lambda}\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda(U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}))=U^{\top}U-I_{T\cdot r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the gradients to zero gives the two necessary optimality conditions:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*}=U_{*}\Lambda_{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*}=U_{*}\Lambda_{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}^{\top}U_{*}=I_{T\cdot r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}^{\top}U_{*}=I_{T\cdot r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The second condition, <a href="#A1.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Optimal Reference Bases ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, holds by construction: we explicitly choose <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> to be an orthonormal matrix. Specifically, we define <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}=[v_{1},\ldots,v_{r},p_{1},\ldots,p_{(T-1)\cdot r}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}=[v_{1},\ldots,v_{r},p_{1},\ldots,p_{(T-1)\cdot r}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{i}\}_{i=1}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{i}\}_{i=1}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthonormal eigenvectors of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with its nonzero eigenvalues <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{j}\}_{j=1}^{(T-1)\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{j}\}_{j=1}^{(T-1)\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> are additional orthonormal vectors chosen to complete the basis.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, to verify the first condition reported in <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Optimal Reference Bases ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we define the diagonal matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{*}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r},0,\ldots,0)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{*}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{r},0,\ldots,0)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\cdot r\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the trailing zeros correspond to the eigenvalues associated with the orthogonal complement. Since each <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> with eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the nullspace of that matrix, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v_{i}=\lambda_{i}v_{i}\quad\text{for }i=1,\dots,r,\quad\text{and}\quad U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}p_{j}=0\quad\text{for }j=1,\dots,(T-1)\cdot r." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v_{i}=\lambda_{i}v_{i}\quad\text{for }i=1,\dots,r,\quad\text{and}\quad U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}p_{j}=0\quad\text{for }j=1,\dots,(T-1)\cdot r.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*}=[\lambda_{1}v_{1},\dots,\lambda_{r}v_{r},0,\dots,0]=U_{*}\Lambda_{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*}=[\lambda_{1}v_{1},\dots,\lambda_{r}v_{r},0,\dots,0]=U_{*}\Lambda_{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">which confirms that the first-order condition in <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Optimal Reference Bases ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> is satisfied.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we substitute this result into the original expression to obtain the optimal value:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\ast}=\mathrm{tr}(U_{*}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*})=\mathrm{tr}(U_{*}^{\top}U_{*}\Lambda_{*})=\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda_{*})=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top})=r," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\ast}=\mathrm{tr}(U_{*}^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}U_{*})=\mathrm{tr}(U_{*}^{\top}U_{*}\Lambda_{*})=\mathrm{tr}(\Lambda_{*})=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{tr}(U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top})=r,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">proving that the maximum value of the quadratic problem is <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, and the corresponding alignment error <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Equivalence of eigenspaces. </span> Now we show that, given the matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> from a LoRA-based adaptation, if <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is also, by construction, an eigenvector of <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}=U_{B}^{(t)}\Sigma^{(t)}V_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}=U_{B}^{(t)}\Sigma^{(t)}V_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v\text{ is an eigenvector of }B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is an eigenvector of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v\text{ is an eigenvector of }B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies(B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top})U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=(B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top})\lambda v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies(B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top})U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=(B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top})\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=\lambda B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=\lambda B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">From the second and fourth rows, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding eigenvalue is <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v\text{ is an eigenvector of }B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top},\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is an eigenvector of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v\text{ is an eigenvector of }B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top},\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies B^{(t)}B^{(t)\top}v=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies v^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies v^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.4" class="ltx_p">Since the matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> has rank <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, it has exactly <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> strictly positive singular values, while all other singular values beyond rank <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> are zero. Thus, the matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite. Hence, it must be:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0\implies U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0\implies U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}{\Sigma^{2}}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0\implies U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0\implies U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}v=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.5" class="ltx_p">which confirms that if <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenvector of <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{(t)}U_{B}^{(t)\top}</annotation></semantics></math> with eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS3.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization to Multiple Tasks. </span> This result generalizes directly to the multi-task setting, as defined in the main paper, by applying it to the matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\in\mathrm{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\in\mathrm{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by horizontally stacking the LoRA updates <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> from all tasks <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the optimal reference basis <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{*}=U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{*}=U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (as done in our approach) is given by the left singular vectors of <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained via SVD. This matrix satisfies both orthonormality and the optimality conditions derived above. Defining <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{*}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{T\cdot r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{*}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{T\cdot r})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐁𝐁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, guarantees perfect reconstruction and zero alignment error for all tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Generalization Beyond the <math id="A1.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\leq m,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\leq m,n</annotation></semantics></math> Assumption</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The derivations in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Secs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Alignment Error Quantification ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> and <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Optimal Reference Bases ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> assumed that the total LoRA rank <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r</annotation></semantics></math> is less than both <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show that this assumption is not necessary, and that <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">the reconstruction error remains zero even when <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r&gt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r&gt;m</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intrinsic rank.</span> When <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r&gt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r&gt;m</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>) or <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>), stacking the LoRA matrices still yields reference bases with intrinsic dimensions:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{U}=\mathrm{rank}([B^{(1)},\dots,B^{(T)}])\leq m,\qquad d_{V}=\mathrm{rank}([A^{(1)},\dots,A^{(T)}]^{\top})\leq n," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{U}=\mathrm{rank}([B^{(1)},\dots,B^{(T)}])\leq m,\qquad d_{V}=\mathrm{rank}([A^{(1)},\dots,A^{(T)}]^{\top})\leq n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">since the number of linearly independent directions cannot exceed the number of rows or columns</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can therefore replace the reference bases <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times T\cdot r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times T\cdot r}</annotation></semantics></math> with truncated orthonormal bases:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\text{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d_{U}},\qquad V_{A}^{\text{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{V}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\text{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d_{U}},\qquad V_{A}^{\text{ref}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{V}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">whose columns span the full LoRA update space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Least-Squares Solution.</span>
Rewriting the least-squares problem (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) in terms of the truncated <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B}^{(t)}=\argmin_{R\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{U}\times r}}\big\|U_{B}^{\text{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\big\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B}^{(t)}=\argmin_{R\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{U}\times r}}\big\|U_{B}^{\text{ref}}R-U_{B}^{(t)}\big\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Following the same derivation as in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Least Squares Solutions ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the optimal solution is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B}^{(t)}=(U_{B}^{\text{ref}})^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B}^{(t)}=(U_{B}^{\text{ref}})^{\top}U_{B}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">with an analogous expression for <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{A}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{A}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alignment Error.</span>
Substituting this solution into the error expression of <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Alignment Error Quantification ‣ Appendix A No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> shows that the optimal alignment error remains</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{U}=r-\|(U_{B}^{(t)})^{\top}U_{B}^{\text{ref}}\|_{F}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{U}=r-\|(U_{B}^{(t)})^{\top}U_{B}^{\text{ref}}\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which achieves zero when <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B}^{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B}^{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> spans the column space of all <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the theoretical guarantees extend unchanged to the case <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r&gt;m,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r&gt;m,n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Computational Complexity Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Iso-C Complexity. </span> To assess the time complexity of our approach, we begin by analyzing that of Iso-C <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, to establish a baseline for comparison. For each layer, the Iso-C procedure can be broken down into the following steps:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LoRA <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> full space</span>: Compute <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(t)}=B^{(t)}A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(t)}=B^{(t)}A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, given the matrices <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting complexity is <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Summation</span>: Applying task arithmetic in the full space, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\operatorname{TA}}=\sum_{t}^{T}\Delta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>TA</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\operatorname{TA}}=\sum_{t}^{T}\Delta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, involves a cost of <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SVD computation</span>: Computing the decomposition <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\operatorname{TA}}=U\Sigma V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>TA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\operatorname{TA}}=U\Sigma V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for an <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> matrix has a complexity of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Isotropization</span>: The final step, <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\operatorname{Iso-C}}=U\Sigma_{\operatorname{avg}}V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>Iso</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>avg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\operatorname{Iso-C}}=U\Sigma_{\operatorname{avg}}V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, is dominated by <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, the total cost of Iso-C is dominated by <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m+m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m+m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n</annotation></semantics></math>, then the time complexity of Iso-C is approximately cubic: <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{3}+T\cdot r\cdot n^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{3}+T\cdot r\cdot n^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the number of features.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KnOTS Complexity. </span> Secondly, we analyze the computational cost of the <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KnOTS</span> method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LoRA <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> full space</span>: As in Iso-C, this step has complexity <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Concatenation</span>: Stacking all weight matrices <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W=\left[\Delta W^{(1)},\dots,\Delta W^{(T)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W=\left[\Delta W^{(1)},\dots,\Delta W^{(T)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> as block columns of a global matrix has a time complexity of <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SVD computation</span>: This is performed on a matrix of size <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times(n\cdot T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times(n\cdot T)</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in a complexity of <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{2}\cdot T^{2}\cdot m+m^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{2}\cdot T^{2}\cdot m+m^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, by making use of the transpose trick<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{SVD}(P^{\top})=U^{{}^{\prime}}\Sigma^{{}^{\prime}}{V^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top}\rightarrow P=(U^{{}^{\prime}}\Sigma^{{}^{\prime}}{V^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top})^{\top}={V^{{}^{\prime}}}\Sigma{U^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>SVD</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mmultiscripts><mi>V</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SVD}(P^{\top})=U^{{}^{\prime}}\Sigma^{{}^{\prime}}{V^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top}\rightarrow P=(U^{{}^{\prime}}\Sigma^{{}^{\prime}}{V^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top})^{\top}={V^{{}^{\prime}}}\Sigma{U^{{}^{\prime}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus, if <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\ll n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\ll n</annotation></semantics></math>, this will reduce the number of operations. We will apply the transpose trick throughout.</span></span></span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Merge</span>: Assuming simple task arithmetic is performed in the <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> space, <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> blocks of <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> columns each are summed, yielding a complexity of <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T^{2}\cdot r\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T^{2}\cdot r\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math> to compute <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\operatorname{merge}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>merge</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\operatorname{merge}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reconstruction</span>: The final step <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\operatorname{KNOTS}}=U\Sigma V_{\operatorname{merge}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>KNOTS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>merge</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\operatorname{KNOTS}}=U\Sigma V_{\operatorname{merge}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> has a complexity of <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m\cdot n\cdot T\cdot r+T\cdot r\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m\cdot n\cdot T\cdot r+T\cdot r\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, the total cost of KNOTS is dominated by <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{3}+T\cdot n(2r\cdot m+m+n\cdot T\cdot m+T\cdot r+r))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{3}+T\cdot n(2r\cdot m+m+n\cdot T\cdot m+T\cdot r+r))</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n</annotation></semantics></math>, the time complexity simplifies to <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{3}T^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{3}T^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Compared to Iso-C, the time complexity of KNOTS remains cubic with respect to the number of features. However, it includes an additional <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> factor that scales quadratically with the number of tasks being merged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TSV Complexity. </span> Then we analyze the cost of TSV <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LoRA <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> full space</span>: As previously, this step has complexity <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot n\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SVD Computation</span>: In this step SVD is performed on <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> matrices of size <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> resulting in a complexity of <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Concatenation</span>: Stacking the first <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> components of left and right singular vectors for all tasks results in <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot k(n+m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot k(n+m))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Global SVD Computation</span>: The SVD performed on the stacked matrices <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times m</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(2\cdot(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(2\cdot(m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Obtaining orthogonal matrices</span>: This step requires <math id="A2.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(2\cdot m^{2}\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(2\cdot m^{2}\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Merge</span>: The final merge has a complexity of <math id="A2.I3.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m\cdot n\cdot T\cdot r+T\cdot r\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m\cdot n\cdot T\cdot r+T\cdot r\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">The overall cost of TSV is thus <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot m\cdot n+T\cdot r\cdot n+T\cdot m^{2}\cdot n+T\cdot n^{3}+T\cdot k\cdot m+T\cdot k\cdot n+m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r\cdot m\cdot n+T\cdot r\cdot n+T\cdot m^{2}\cdot n+T\cdot n^{3}+T\cdot k\cdot m+T\cdot k\cdot n+m^{2}\cdot n+n^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,r,k\ll n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,r,k\ll n</annotation></semantics></math>, the computational cost is dominated by <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot n^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Core Space Complexity. </span> Finally, we analyze the cost of our approach in <span id="A2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Core Space</span>.</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Stacking <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></span>: Stacking two sequences of <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> matrices – one with each matrix of shape <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times n</annotation></semantics></math> and the other with each matrix of shape <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times r</annotation></semantics></math> – results in a cost of <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r(n+m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot r(n+m))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SVD computation</span>: The stacked global <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> matrix has shape <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T\cdot r)\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T\cdot r)\times n</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, the cost of its SVD is <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{2}\cdot(T\cdot r)+(T\cdot r)^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{2}\cdot(T\cdot r)+(T\cdot r)^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, by using the transpose trick. The stacked <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> matrix has shape <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times(T\cdot r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times(T\cdot r)</annotation></semantics></math>, with a cost of <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot(T\cdot r)+(T\cdot r)^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}\cdot(T\cdot r)+(T\cdot r)^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The overall cost of this step is <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((m^{2}+n^{2})\cdot(T\cdot r)+2\cdot(T\cdot r)^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((m^{2}+n^{2})\cdot(T\cdot r)+2\cdot(T\cdot r)^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Low-rank loop</span>: In the optimized version of the low-rank loop, we only compute the matrix multiplication to obtain the aligned matrices. In this case the total cost is <math id="A2.I4.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot(Tmr^{2}+Tr^{2}n+T^{2}r^{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot(Tmr^{2}+Tr^{2}n+T^{2}r^{3}))</annotation></semantics></math> (using the optimal matrix multiplication order <math id="A2.I4.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}B)(AV_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ref</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{B}^{\mathrm{ref}}B)(AV_{A}^{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>). Assuming that <math id="A2.I4.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,r&lt;&lt;n,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,r&lt;&lt;n,m</annotation></semantics></math>, the cost is dominated by <math id="A2.I4.i2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T^{2}r^{2}(m+n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T^{2}r^{2}(m+n))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Merge:</span> Assuming simple task arithmetic is performed in the aligned core space, the cost is <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T^{3}\cdot r^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T^{3}\cdot r^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Isotropization:</span> Optionally, Iso-C can be applied in the core space; since the core space is defined within a square matrix of dimension <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot r\times T\cdot r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot r\times T\cdot r</annotation></semantics></math>, this step adds an additional time complexity of <math id="A2.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T^{3}r^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T^{3}r^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reconstruction:</span> The final step requires <math id="A2.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m\cdot T^{2}\cdot r^{2}+m\cdot T\cdot r\cdot n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m\cdot T^{2}\cdot r^{2}+m\cdot T\cdot r\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">To sum up, our approach involves:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{Tr(n+m)}_{\text{Stacking}}+\underbrace{Tr(m^{2}+n^{2})+2(Tr)^{3}}_{\text{SVD refs.}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Stacking</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>SVD refs.</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{Tr(n+m)}_{\text{Stacking}}+\underbrace{Tr(m^{2}+n^{2})+2(Tr)^{3}}_{\text{SVD refs.}}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{(T^{2}r^{2}(m+n))}_{\text{Low-rank loop.}}+\underbrace{Tr(T^{2}r+Trm+mn)}_{\text{Merge \&amp; Rec.}})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Low-rank loop.</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Merge &amp; Rec.</mtext></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{(T^{2}r^{2}(m+n))}_{\text{Low-rank loop.}}+\underbrace{Tr(T^{2}r+Trm+mn)}_{\text{Merge \&amp; Rec.}})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Tr(m+n+2m^{2}+2n^{2}+mn+r^{2})+T^{2}r^{2}(2m+n+T)+T^{3}r^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Tr(m+n+2m^{2}+2n^{2}+mn+r^{2})+T^{2}r^{2}(2m+n+T)+T^{3}r^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">If we assume that <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n</annotation></semantics></math>, the total time complexity simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Tr(2n+5n^{2}+r^{2})+T^{2}r^{2}(3n+T)+T^{3}r^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Tr(2n+5n^{2}+r^{2})+T^{2}r^{2}(3n+T)+T^{3}r^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.2" class="ltx_p">which, if we assume <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,r\ll n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,r\ll n</annotation></semantics></math>, is dominated by:</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Trn^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Trn^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Analysis</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>High subspace alignment leads to lower interference</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this Section, we experimentally show that merging in Core Space reduces interference when merging models. We follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> and measure the interference as the L1 distance between the final embeddings of task-specific models and the merged one. We compare the interference when merging with TSV + Iso-C in Full Space versus Core Space. For each dataset, we collect the activations from the final layer (<em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, the projection to a common vision-language space) of both the task-specific model and the merged model. We present the average distance across all the samples in the test set. We observe lower interference when merging in Core Space, highlighting its effectiveness. Note that Full Space merging, which causes higher interference, also exhibits higher SAR in <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17786v1/distances_tsv_iso_full_vs_tsv_iso_core.svg" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:467/276;" width="467" height="276"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Mean L1 distance between the final embeddings of task-specific models and the merged one using TSV + Iso in Full and Core space. We used ViT-B/16 model.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Rank of the merged update matrices</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=8</annotation></semantics></math> ViT-B/32 models fine-tuned with LoRA of rank <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=16</annotation></semantics></math>. The merged update matrices <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math> resulting from different merging methods and spaces can have different effective ranks <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\Delta W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\Delta W}</annotation></semantics></math>. Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ C.2 Rank of the merged update matrices ‣ Appendix C Additional Analysis ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports the average rank of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math> across all layers.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Average rank <math id="A3.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\Delta W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\Delta W}</annotation></semantics></math> of merged update matrices <math id="A3.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by merging 8 ViT-B/32 LoRA models with <math id="A3.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=16</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A3.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Tr=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Tr=128</annotation></semantics></math>).</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Merging Space</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TA</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TSV</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T6.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TIES</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Full</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">766.25</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">KnOTS</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">128.00</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Core</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">128.00</td>
<td id="A3.T6.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">128.00</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In most cases, the target rank of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Tr=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Tr=128</annotation></semantics></math>. The only exception is merging with TIES in Full space, where for weight matrices <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> the effective rank approaches the dimensionality of the matrices <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\min(m,n)=768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\min(m,n)=768</annotation></semantics></math>. This phenomenon arises because TIES performs trimming on the reconstructed weight matrices <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{t}=BA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{t}=BA</annotation></semantics></math>, which destroys the low-rank structure. In contrast, both Core and KnOTS operate directly in a constrained <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Tr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Tr</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space, ensuring that the merged <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math> maintains the intended rank.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
