<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Optimized Pipeline</h3>

<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17786v1/method_optimized.svg" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/219;" width="286" height="219"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>The proposed <span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Core Space Merging</span> with the optimized algorithm. First, we perform SVD on a concatenation of low-dimensional <math id="A4.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices to obtain reference bases. Afterwards, we directly compute the aligned core matrices. Finally, we perform merging in the Core Space and reconstruct to obtain the final <math id="A4.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report in <a href="#A4.F7" title="In D.1 Optimized Pipeline ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiment Details ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> the illustration of the Core Space approach with the optimized pipeline presented in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 No Information Loss in Core Space Representation ‣ 4 The Core Space Merging Framework ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Experimental Environment</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The language experiments with Llama 3 8B were performed with a single 48G NVIDIA L40S. In contrast, the more affordable vision experiments were executed using a single 16G NVIDIA RTX 4080. To keep things fair, the reported times for the language experiments all refer to experiments performed on the same machine.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our implementation builds directly on the KnOTS codebase <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> and uses the exact LoRA checkpoints they released. For full details on the original training and adaptation procedures, please refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Hyperparameter Search</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To find optimal hyperparameters for each model, we adopt the widely used validation holdout strategy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>. Specifically, we perform a linear search for hyperparameters on the validation set, starting from a defined minimum value and incrementally increasing it until performance declines, indicating the optimal range. The identified optimal hyperparameters are then applied to the test set. We use the following search settings:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scaling factor <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> starts at <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, increasing in increments of <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. This is used for every approach.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The top-<math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> parameter for TIES and DARE-TIES begins at <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> and increases in increments of <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pruning factor <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> for DARE-TIES starts at <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and increases in increments of <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For CART, the pruning rank is searched over the set <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.04,0.08,0.16,0.32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.04,0.08,0.16,0.32\}</annotation></semantics></math>, following the methodology of the original paper. Additionally, CART includes an extra scaling factor <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in its merging formulation. Specifically, the merged weights are computed as <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{merged}}=W_{0}+\alpha(\theta_{\text{avg}}+\lambda\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bar{\tau}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>merged</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{merged}}=W_{0}+\alpha(\theta_{\text{avg}}+\lambda\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bar{\tau}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{avg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{avg}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the average of the updates and <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\tau}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\tau}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the centered task vector for task <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. For further details, we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A4.T7" title="In D.3 Hyperparameter Search ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiment Details ‣ Accurate and Efficient Low-Rank Model Merging in Core Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we report the parameters used for the various merging methods in Core Space across all backbones. Note that we search for the optimal parameters for all methods across all spaces to maintain fairness. For the natural-language inference experiments, we omit CART as its hyperparameter tuning proved prohibitively expensive and exclude <span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">+Iso-C</span> variants, as they consistently degraded performance.</p>
</div>
